+--------------------------------+-------------------------------------------+
| DHF-HRC-0003, Rev.2            | Heracles Software Verification Plan (SVP) |
+--------------------------------+-------------------------------------------+
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: RQ-H1FWMC-
TITLE: Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-1
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 11: Termination
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall terminate an ongoing emission upon receipt of a stop command from
the PC
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-2
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Head Interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to receive IO feedback values from the head interface board
including button press toggles
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-3
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Head Interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor communication with the head interface board and report a
fault if no valid communication is received within 0.5 seconds
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-6
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Fault information
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to respond to a request from the PC with information about the
fault which triggered the transition into fault mode, including:

- The type of fault occurrence
- The state in which the fault occurred
- The expected vs measured conditions which triggered the fault
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-7
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Emission indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall enable an external emission indicator during the emission state when
there is an ongoing emission
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-8
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Interlocks
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the status of the system interlocks and throw a fault if any
interlocks are in an invalid condition. Interlocks include:

- E-stops
- Ion pump HV interlocks
- KUKA robot arm interlocks
- Door interlock
- Coolant level sensor
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-9
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Coils
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the focus coil feedback current values and report a fault for
values that are more than 150 mA out of tolerance.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-10
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Backup Timer
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the backup timer communication and report a fault if the
communication has been corrupted
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-11
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Backup Timer
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor communication with the backup timers and report a fault if
the timers do not respond
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-12
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 01: Filament conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall report a fault if the HVPS has not reached the target filament current
setpoint during the conditioning procedure within a timeout period of 360 seconds
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-13
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 02: Warmup procedure
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall report a fault if the HVPS has not reached the target filament setpoint
during the warmup procedure within a timeout period of 180 seconds
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-14
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 07: Operational point setup
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall report a fault if the HVPS has not reached the target kV setpoint during
the operational point setup processes within a timeout period of 90 seconds
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-15
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Operation 10 - Emission
STATEMENT: >>>
During an emission, the firmware shall monitor the high voltage feedback from the HVPS
and report a fault if it deviates by more than 5% from the desired target specified in the
treatment plan.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-16
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 09: Initiation
STATEMENT: >>>
On the initiation of an operational point emission execution, the firmware shall direct the
HV interface board to ramp up the filament current to the specified setpoint in the
treatment plan prior to allowing emission (dropping the grid).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-17
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 08: Ready
STATEMENT: >>>
For the operational points which are NOT the first executions of a treatment plan (whether
an initial run or resumed plan), the firmware shall utilize the auto-execute parameter in
the treatment plan to determine if the emission of the point should be automatically
executed without requiring PC intervention.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-18
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 08: Ready
STATEMENT: >>>
For the first operational point in the execution of a treatment plan (whether an initial run
or resumed plan), the firmware shall remain in the ready state and not proceed with
emission until receiving an initiation command from the PC.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-19
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 07: Operational point setup
STATEMENT: >>>
Prior to the execution of an operational point emission, the firmware shall verify that the
HV ramping of the HVPS has terminated and the target kV has been reached
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-20
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 07: Operational point setup
STATEMENT: >>>
Prior to the execution of a treatment plan operational point emission, the firmware shall
direct the HV interface board to the targeted kV setpoint
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-21
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 06 - HVPS Check
STATEMENT: >>>
On the release of treatment plan for execution, the firmware shall cycle the HVPS
interlocks and notify the HV interface board
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-22
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 02: Warmup procedure
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to an invalid warmup procedure request from the PC with an
error reply indicating invalid values have been received. Invalid parameters are those
which cannot be processed or are formatted improperly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-23
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment plan reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond with an out of bounds error message if the PC sends an out of
bounds request for the operational point parameters of a treatment plan. A valid request
will be the operational point index value, between 0 and 62.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-24
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 04: Treatment plan confirmation
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall not consider a treatment plan as a whole to be confirmed unless all
operational points are each individually confirmed, without interruption of standby
timeout or system faults. Individual operational points will be considered confirmed on
receipt of confirmation parameters which match staged parameters
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-25
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 05: Treatment plan release
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall not proceed with the release of a treatment plan for execution if all
interlocks are not ready for emission
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-26
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 05: Treatment plan release
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to invalid treatment plan release request from the PC with an
error reply indicating an invalid request. A treatment plan release request will be
considered invalid if the system is not in the staged state with a confirmed treatment plan.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-27
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 04: Treatment plan confirmation
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to incorrect treatment plan operational point confirmation
parameters from the PC with an error reply indicating incorrect values have been received.
Incorrect parameters are values which do not match staged parameters
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-28
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 04: Treatment plan confirmation
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to invalid treatment plan operational point confirmation
parameters from the PC with an error reply indicating invalid values have been received.
Invalid parameters are those which cannot be processed or are formatted improperly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-29
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 04: Treatment plan confirmation
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to out of bounds treatment plan operational point
confirmation parameters from the PC with an error reply indicating out of bounds values
have been received. Out of bounds values are those which are outside of the range of
acceptable values. Acceptable values will be:

- Acceleration potential (kV), range 0 to 100 kV
- Emission current (mA), range 0 to 1 mA
- Total delivery time, range 0 to 300 seconds
- Remaining delivery time, range 0 to total delivery time
- Beam optic focus adjustment values, range 0 to 3A
- Beam optic deflection adjustment values, range -1.5A to +1.5A
- Filament current (mA), range 0 to 3999 mA
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-30
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 04: Treatment plan confirmation
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall acknowledge the receipt of valid treatment plan operational point
confirmation parameters received from the PC. A valid treatment plan includes the
following parameters for an operational point:

- Acceleration potential (kV), range 0 to 100 kV
- Emission current (mA), range 0 to 1 mA
- Total delivery time, range 0 to 300 seconds
- Remaining delivery time, range 0 to total delivery time
- Beam optic focus adjustment values, range 0 to 3A
- Beam optic deflection adjustment values, range -1.5A to +1.5A
- Filament current (mA), range 0 to 3999 mA
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-31
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 04: Treatment plan confirmation
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall accept confirmation of treatment plan operational points from the PC
after the staging process has been completed, responding with an error message if
operational point confirmation is attempted outside of this confirmation process
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-32
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 03.1: Treatment staging - new session commencement
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall, upon the receipt of a valid command for the beginning of a new
staging, generate and relay a session ID as a response to the PC. A staging request from
the PC includes the total number of operational points for the plan, ranging from 1 to 5
points and is received during the primed state.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-33
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 01: Filament conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall only be able to perform filament conditioning from a 'cold' state
where there is no filament current present, and shall reply to filament condition requests
outside of this cold state with an error response
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-34
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 01: Filament conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to an invalid filament target value in a filament conditioning
request from the PC with an invalid value response. Invalid parameters are those which
cannot be processed or are formatted improperly.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-35
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 01: Filament conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to an out of bounds target value in a filament conditioning
request with an out of bounds value response. An out of bounds parameter is outside of
the range of acceptable values, which is 2000 to 4000 mA
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-36
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 01: Filament conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to perform the filament conditioning as a response to a PC
request, which specifies the target filament current
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-37
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 01: Filament conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to perform a filament conditioning process, in which the
filament current is ramped up to a target value before ramping back down to off
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-38
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 00: Startup
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall transition out of the startup state once it receives an initialize
command from the PC, and enter the cold state
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-39
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 00: Startup
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall begin in a startup state on board power on
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-40
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 03.1: Treatment staging - new session commencement
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to an out-of-bound new staging session request from the PC
with an error reply indicating out-of-bound values have been received. An out of bounds
parameter is outside of the range of acceptable values, 1 to 5 points
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-41
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 02: Warmup procedure
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to an out of bounds warmup request from the PC with an error reply indicating out of bounds values have been received. An out of bounds parameter is outside of the range of acceptable values. A warmup valid request will contain a target filament current value for the warmup that is between 2000 mA and 3500 mA
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-42
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 03.1: Treatment staging - new session commencement
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to begin treatment plan staging only from the primed state,
responding with an error message if establishment of a new staging session is attempted outside of this state
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-43
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 03.2: Treatment staging
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall only accept the loading of a treatment plan from the PC during a
designated staging process, responding to the GUI with an error value if the treatment
plan loading is attempted outside of this staging process
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-44
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 03.2: Treatment staging
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to invalid treatment plan staging parameters from the PC with an error reply indicating invalid values have been received. Invalid values are values which cannot be processed, or which are formatted incorrectly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-45
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 03.2: Treatment staging
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond to out of bounds treatment plan staging parameters from the
PC with an error reply indicating out of bounds values have been received. An out of
bounds parameter is outside of the range of acceptable values
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-46
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: PC Ethernet commands
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall respond with an 'unrecognized message' response when it receives a
command which is either not formatted properly or not recognized.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-47
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: USB
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to erase a predetermined area of flash memory, corresponding to application CRC verification area when requested by the PC over USB.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-48
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: USB
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to jump to execution of the bootloader application when
requested by the PC over USB.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-49
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: USB
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control application firmware shall be able to receive and process commands
from PC via the board's USB connection.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-52
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Backup Timer
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall have the ability to read and report the current backup timer countdown value.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-53
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Backup Timer
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall have the ability to set and initialize the backup timer ICs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-54
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Coils
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the deflection coil feedback current values and report a fault
for values that are more than 50 mA out of tolerance from the expected setpoint output
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-55
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Coils
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to set the deflection and focus coil setpoint control signals.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-60
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Coolant monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the reported coolant temperature and report a fault if the
temperature is above 35C
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-61
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Coolant monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the reported coolant system flow rate and report a fault if the
rate is below 2 LPM or above 6 LPM when the coolant pump is enabled.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-62
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Head Interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to receive cooling system feedback values from the head
interface board.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-63
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Temperature monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall adjust the heatsink fan speed based on the heatsink temperature
feedback in order to provide additional cooling when temperatures increase.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-64
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Temperature monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the Peltier heatsink temperature and report a fault when it is
above 55C
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-65
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Temperature monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall adjust the system cabinet fan speed based on the cabinet temperature
feedback in order to provide additional cooling when temperatures increase.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-66
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Temperature monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the system cabinet temperature and report a fault when it is
above 50C
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-68
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: HVPS Interface Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor communication with the HVPS interface board and report a
fault if no communication is received for no longer than 1 second
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-69
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 12: Discharge
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall return the system into a cold state if the system has been idle in primed
state for a period of 5 minutes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-70
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 09: Initiation
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall set the deflection coil and focus coil outputs to the target setpoint
values from the treatment plan, prior to the start of each operational point emission
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-71
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Undesired emission monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the cathode current feedback from the HVPS and report a fault
if the value is above 0.2 mA when the system is not in 'Emission' state
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-72
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 10 - Emission
STATEMENT: >>>
When an emission begins, the firmware shall transmit a starting condition to the two
backup timers.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-73
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 10 - Emission
STATEMENT: >>>
When an emission begins, the firmware shall begin an internal timer to serve as the
treatment point delivery duration.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-74
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 05: Treatment plan release
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall, on request from the PC, release a treatment plan from the staged
state for execution, if a treatment plan has been successfully staged and confirmed
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-75
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Operation 10 - Emission
STATEMENT: >>>
During an emission, the firmware shall monitor the cathode current feedback from the
HVPS and report a fault if it deviates by more than 5% from the desired target specified in
the treatment plan.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-76
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 02: Warmup procedure
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to perform a warmup procedure from the cold state if a valid
warmup request is received from the PC. A warmup request will contain a target filament
current value for the warmup that is between 2000 mA and 3500 mA
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-77
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Fault mode
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall terminate any ongoing emission whenever a fault mode is entered.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-78
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Fault information
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to clear latched fault flags when requested by the PC.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-79
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Fault information
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall latch fault condition flags
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-80
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Fault mode
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control application firmware shall enter a fault mode when a fault is detected.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-81
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment plan reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control application firmware shall be able to reply to the PC on a request for the
currently programmed treatment plan parameters of a specified operational point,
responding with the operational point parameters on receipt of a valid request. A valid
request will be the operational point index value, between 0 and 62.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-82
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 03.2: Treatment staging
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall acknowledge the receipt of valid treatment plan staging parameters
received from the PC. A valid treatment plan includes the following parameter types for an
operational point:

- Acceleration potential (kV), range 0 to 100 kV
- Emission current (mA), range 0 to 1 mA
- Total delivery time, range 0 to 300 seconds
- Remaining delivery time, range 0 to total delivery time
- Beam optic focus adjustment values, range 0 to 3A
- Beam optic deflection adjustment values, range -1.5A to +1.5A
- Filament current (mA), range 0 to 3999 mA
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-83
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Report telemetry to PC
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall report monitored system parameter values in response to a telemetry
request from the PC. Parameter types in the response include the following:

- Control board state
- Current system operational point in treatment plan
- Total operational points in treatment plan
- Internal timer value
- Backup timer values
- Feedback values
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-84
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: PC Ethernet commands
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to respond to commands received from a PC over Ethernet.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-85
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 11: Termination
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall revert to the staged state after the cessation of a treatment plan.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-86
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 12: Discharge
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall return the system into a cold state if the system has been idle in the
ready state for a period of 2 minutes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-87
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Operation 12: Discharge
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall return the system into a cold state if the system has been idle in staged
state for a period of 5 minutes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWMC-305
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: QC Processing
STATEMENT: >>>
The Main Control App FW shall be able to accept QC Diode values from the Head Interface
FW and process them for output to the PC Application. A QC ping command should also be
processed when received from the PC application.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
